        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lower Park Creek Patrol Cabin, Glacier National Park, Montana, Alberta, British Columbia\n- Structures: backcountry log cabin\n- Topics: national parks, geography, natural features\n\nFacts:\n- The Lower Park Creek Patrol Cabin is a rustic backcountry log cabin in Glacier National Park.\n- The Lower Park Creek Patrol Cabin was built in 1925 and has a single room.\n- Glacier National Park is a national park in Montana on the Canada–United States border with Alberta and British Columbia.\n- Glacier National Park encompasses over 1 million acres, includes parts of two Rocky Mountain sub-ranges, has over 130 named lakes, contains more than 1,000 plant species, and supports hundreds of animal species.",
